From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
Date: Tue, 1 Sep 2026 15:38:42 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm/dpu: cmd mode: send the pageflip event at rd_ptr, not
 transfer end

On command-mode panels the pageflip event was only delivered once the whole
DSI transfer had completed (pp_done). wlroots waits for that event before
rendering the next frame, so the session was locked to half the panel rate:
measured on taimen (Pixel 2 XL), a 14.6 ms transfer inside a 16.7 ms TE slot
with the flip at +14.6 ms gave rock-steady 33.4 ms frame callbacks, in the UI
as well as in video.

The read pointer has already started this frame's transfer, so the previous
framebuffer is unreferenced by then -- the pageflip semantic. rd_ptr is
already the cmd-mode vblank source, and DRM delivers pageflip events at
vblank, so this also brings msm in line with that convention.

An earlier attempt used the CTL_START interrupt. That cannot work on msm8998,
which has no such interrupt (INTR2 bits 9..13 assert only from sdm845 on), so
the handler was never even registered. rd_ptr exists on this SoC and is
already wired up.

Gated on pending_kickoff_cnt so a bare TE tick with no commit in flight does
not release a buffer the panel is still being fed from.

Signed-off-by: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_crtc.c      | 11 ++++++++++
 drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_encoder.h   |  1 +
 .../drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_encoder_phys_cmd.c  | 21 +++++++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 33 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_crtc.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_crtc.c
index 42d0a529b4d5..d959b7dc12a2 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_crtc.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_crtc.c
@@ -723,6 +723,17 @@ void dpu_crtc_frame_event_cb(struct drm_crtc *crtc, u32 event)
 	if (event & DPU_ENCODER_FRAME_EVENT_IDLE)
 		return;
 
+	/*
+	 * Frame latched into the panel transfer (cmd mode): send the pending
+	 * pageflip now so userspace can pipeline the next frame into the
+	 * ongoing transfer. complete_commit()'s later call is a no-op once
+	 * the event has been sent.
+	 */
+	if (event & DPU_ENCODER_FRAME_EVENT_STARTED) {
+		_dpu_crtc_complete_flip(crtc);
+		return;
+	}
+
 	dpu_crtc = to_dpu_crtc(crtc);
 	priv = crtc->dev->dev_private;
 	crtc_id = drm_crtc_index(crtc);
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_encoder.h b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_encoder.h
index 4942097e7613..3964bb185129 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_encoder.h
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_encoder.h
@@ -16,6 +16,7 @@
 #define DPU_ENCODER_FRAME_EVENT_ERROR			BIT(1)
 #define DPU_ENCODER_FRAME_EVENT_PANEL_DEAD		BIT(2)
 #define DPU_ENCODER_FRAME_EVENT_IDLE			BIT(3)
+#define DPU_ENCODER_FRAME_EVENT_STARTED		BIT(4)
 
 #define IDLE_TIMEOUT	(66 - 16/2)
 
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_encoder_phys_cmd.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_encoder_phys_cmd.c
index 45079ee59cf6..0e03b1746afe 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_encoder_phys_cmd.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_encoder_phys_cmd.c
@@ -121,6 +121,27 @@ static void dpu_encoder_phys_cmd_te_rd_ptr_irq(void *arg)
 
 	dpu_encoder_vblank_callback(phys_enc->parent, phys_enc);
 
+	/*
+	 * The read pointer has started this frame's transfer, so the previous
+	 * framebuffer is no longer referenced -- which is the pageflip event
+	 * semantic. Delivering it here rather than at transfer *completion*
+	 * lets the compositor render the next frame while this one is still
+	 * being pushed over DSI. Without it the whole session is locked to
+	 * half the panel rate: a 14.6 ms transfer inside a 16.7 ms TE slot,
+	 * with the flip at +14.6 ms, serialises everything to 33.4 ms.
+	 *
+	 * Gated on a kickoff being in flight: the tearcheck read pointer also
+	 * ticks on bare TE with no commit pending, and signalling a flip then
+	 * would release a buffer the panel is still being fed from.
+	 *
+	 * MSM8998 cannot use the CTL_START interrupt for this -- it has none
+	 * (see dpu_3_0_msm8998.h) -- but rd_ptr is already its vblank source,
+	 * and DRM delivers pageflip events at vblank anyway.
+	 */
+	if (atomic_read(&phys_enc->pending_kickoff_cnt))
+		dpu_encoder_frame_done_callback(phys_enc->parent, phys_enc,
+						DPU_ENCODER_FRAME_EVENT_STARTED);
+
 	atomic_add_unless(&cmd_enc->pending_vblank_cnt, -1, 0);
 	wake_up_all(&cmd_enc->pending_vblank_wq);
 	DPU_ATRACE_END("rd_ptr_irq");
